{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1786429211,"nonce":"HsA32oyvfmVD7MqzAZk6RfhDNB8=","message":"PARTIAL — budget ran out mid-task, but G1 EXISTS AND IS ALREADY EARNING ITS KEEP.\n\nG1 (Go DTO -\u003e OpenAPI) is implemented in test/contract/dto_schema_test.go and reflects over the real structs. It went from 152 raw complaints down to 6 genuine divergences, and it caught a bug introduced THE SAME DAY:\n  - AlertDTO.synthetic: the contract declares it REQUIRED; no Go json tag produces it, so the server never sends it (from the delivery-drills work).\n  - MatcherDTO.value: contract says required; the Go request struct accepts a body without it.\n  - NotificationDTO.updated_at and NotificationDetailDTO.updated_at: the contract permits null; Go declares a non-pointer time.Time that can never marshal to null.\n  - NotificationDetailDTO.delivery_summary: Go has omitempty so the key vanishes when empty, but the contract lists it in required.\n  - rules.RuleExprDiffDTO: the contract declares a 3-branch oneOf; G1 cannot diff one Go struct against a union — the schema needs splitting or the Go type binding to one branch.\nA companion query-parameter check found 6 more, including two operations declaring a `label` query parameter that NO Go field reads (setting it does nothing) and three Go query objects whose operations do not exist in the contract at all.\n\nG4: web/src/api/generated/validators.ts is generated and checked in, but the migration of the hand-written valibot schemas onto it is incomplete and the gen:validators/CI wiring is unfinished.\nG2: not started — the schemathesis-vs-Go-native decision was not reached.\n\nNOT DONE, and it is this issue's stated acceptance criterion: none of the gates has been demonstrated to fail against a deliberately planted drift and then pass after revert. G1's real findings above are strong evidence it works, but that is not the same as the planted-drift demonstration this issue asks for.","files":null}]}